# Automated Machine Learning: Tuning Neural Networks with Bayesian Optimization and GPyOpt

![Bayesian Optimization Workflow](https://github.com/paulineonier/holbertonschool-machine_learning/blob/main/unsupervised_learning/hyperparameter_tuning/6-bayes_opt.py)

When training deep neural networks, selecting the right hyperparameters often feels more like black magic than science. Should you use a learning rate of 0.001 or 0.0003? Is 64 units enough for a hidden layer, or do you need 256? 

While techniques like **Grid Search** test combinations exhaustively and **Random Search** samples points blindly, **Bayesian Optimization** offers an intelligent, probabilistic approach that finds optimal parameters with significantly fewer function evaluations.

